      "abstract": "\nThis article treats the theme of secularisation in Michael Rosen\u2019s The Shadow of God. It addresses the persistence of Christian metaphysical precepts in Kant and their transformation in Hegel. The argument focuses on both thinkers\u2019 ideas of freedom, obligation and immortality. In the process, it recovers the import of Hegel\u2019s understanding of Geist as the dynamic element in his philosophy of history. I conclude by showing that Hegel\u2019s commitment to a form of pluralism is compatible with his defence of a hierarchy of civilisational norms.",
